    <p class="eyebrow">Iterate hackathon, Track 4: World Models</p>
    <h1>How long can a generated world hold together while an agent plays in it?</h1>
    <p class="lede">An AI world model turns key presses into video of a world you can move through. We take an open one, LingBot-World v2, and add memory and tracking while it runs, with no retraining. On the <a href="https://kxding.github.io/project/PlayWorld/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PlayWorld</a> benchmark, an AI player plays 171 tasks in these worlds and Google's Gemini scores each video from 1 to 5. This page updates live.</p>
